    "category": "Indicator",
    "type_designations": ["260/290 Series", "Target 260S", "Target 260D", "Status 290P", "Status 290S"],
    "module_designation": null,
    "description": "Family of indicating devices designed to be used as part of a single-interval Class III or IIII non-automatic weighing instrument. Self-indicating, mains or DC powered, LED display, 4 function keys. Not designed for direct sales to the public. Plastic enclosure (wall-mounted Target 260S, Target 260D, Status 290P) or stainless steel enclosure (desktop Status 290S). External connectors on the Target 260D; internal connectors via glands on Target 260S, Status 290P and Status 290S. Devices: semi-automatic zero setting (<= 4% Max), semi-automatic subtractive tare weighing, gross/net indication, zero-indicator, indication of stable equilibrium, net indicator, printing. Interfaces: load cell connection, analogue output with RS232, CAN Bus, Profibus DP, Ethernet TCP/IP, Ethernet IP, Profinet, EtherCAT, relay output (3), digital input (2). Any compatible load cell with a valid OIML R60 Certificate of Conformity may be used, subject to the manufacturer's compatibility of modules calculation; a load cell marked NH is allowed only if humidity testing to R76 has been conducted. Access to electronics and USB port secured by tamper-evident label; load cell connection (and junction box when applicable) secured by wire-and-seal or tamper-evident label. Firmware download only possible via the sealed USB port."
  },
